I suggest updating to 3.4.3, which was released on early December.
It has most of the 3.4.2 bugs fixed and you can get it from
http://www.nethack.org 

For example C342-23: "Save/restore in explore/debug mode fails under some
OS's.". I never encountered this bug myself, but on Linux I have only
played self-compiled Nethack and I don't know if it matters..

> An attempt at starting the game again resulted in an error message.

When the game crashes, starting it again with the same username before
running recover usually ruins your possible chance for recovering the
crashed game.. 

> Obviously there was plenty of data on the game, and using "recover"
> seemed to work.  I have not played the game anymore to determine if
> something is amiss.

Yep, there's one alock file for every dungeon level you have visited
during that game. The file list looks like you have explored the main
dungeon down to level 19, and all the Sokoban levels and much of the
Mines, maybe all.. and there is even the alock.0 file that normally gets
overwritten first when you start a new game.
Good news is that if the recovered 3.4.2 save file is not corrupted, it
may work with 3.4.3. 
Bad news is that both versions need to have many compile-time options the
same way and if you use a binary packet that was not compiled by the
devteam and downloaded from their site, you can't always easily make sure
about which options it was compiled with.

